  "origin": "Agreement-supplied Danish encyclopedia article corpus from Lex.dk, provided to the Danish Foundation Models project under a Danish Foundation Model agreement whose licensing does not permit public sharing. No Hugging Face identifier exists; the data is not publicly redistributed. Per the Mimir technical report, DFM uses such agreement-supplied datasets to derive synthetic instruction-tuning data rather than training directly on the data. Contributed 313M sampled tokens per epoch to the DFM Mimir v1 corpus (0.44467%). Form: agreement-supplied. The license field carries an interim Sourcelume convention IRI indicating agreement-bound (non-public) terms; the actual terms are private to the DFM-Lex.dk agreement.",
